Hmm but keep the comment about "the ending check runs only for a run that ended of its own accord".

Wait — does a loop abort leave a stopFile? No.

Now, for the loop reask, the injection: `inject_loop_continuation.ts --session session`. The note needs the loop_abort facts. Where does it read them from? The session itself (last atoma_runs entry). So the injector reads the session, extracts the verdict via `loopAbortFromSession`, and writes `loopContinuationMessage(abort)`. 

